# Backups. The convention here is <name>.pre-<what>-<date>, and ktcommit.sh commits
# with `git add -A`, so every backup taken during a session went into a public
# archive: on 2026-09-22 that included a 6.4MB duplicate of the EPUB written by the
# publisher's own deploy step. The deliberate archive/backups-20260922/ folder is
# already tracked and stays tracked; this only stops new ones from being swept in.
*.pre-*
*.pre-update
